# Source and parser redistribution provenance

The VS Code declaration's exact header attributes copyright to Microsoft Corporation and states MIT licensing. The same pinned commit's [official root license](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/07f806f999227108933c2e30515b26eecc1fda74/LICENSE.txt) explicitly permits copying and distributing the software and its associated documentation, subject to retaining the copyright and permission notices. Exact bytes are retained in `source/LICENSE.txt.snapshot`; the source declaration retains its own copyright/license header. The official `package.json` at that same commit independently records MIT licensing and version 1.140.0. The source URLs and byte hashes are in `acquisition.json`.

Those bindings support redistribution of the full retained API declaration and derived source-span/type/comment inventory with the exact MIT notice included. This claim concerns the Code OSS repository source, not the Microsoft Visual Studio Code product binary license, marketplace content, third-party extensions, fonts, or any other artifact. No product executable/archive is included in this study's public subset.

The official `typescript` 5.9.3 npm metadata points to `microsoft/TypeScript` and reports Apache-2.0. Its archive's declared SHA512 SRI and SHA1 digest were verified before selected JavaScript was loaded. Exact package `LICENSE.txt` and `ThirdPartyNoticeText.txt` are retained under `parser/`; selected runtime and archive hashes remain recorded while their actual bytes stay local-only. The archive contains `ThirdPartyNoticeText.txt`, not the initially assumed `NOTICE.txt`. The parser runtime is not proposed for public copying in this subset. Retaining parser provenance/notices does not equate parser execution with original VS Code execution.

The inventory and collector are newly authored. Derived source snippets retain the original MIT provenance. No claim of original-product replacement, clean-room implementation or complete runtime compatibility follows from the licensing permissions or inventory.
